_refine.details                                  
;The crystal with rotational order-disorder pathology is composed of tetramers with 222 symmetry incorporated into the lattice in two different ways, rotated 90 degrees with respect to each other around the crystal c-axis, with tetramer axes coincident with crystallographic 2-fold axes. The random distribution of alternatively oriented tetramers in the crystal creates the rotational Order-Disorder structure with statistically averaged I422 symmetry in which one tetramer overlaps with 90 degree rotated tetramer in the same physical space.
;
